  "text": "It's not easy to fool a betting company, but this might be the dumbest way to do it. Recent advancements in sports betting have allowed for live betting, which is making bets as the games are unfolding in real time. And you don't have to bet on the whole game, you can bet on many little things like who's going to score the next point. Problem is, when someone scores that point, it takes a second or two before the event is registered and updated in the system. So naturally, there are people who try to take advantage of that little delay. They buy tickets to the actual games, go see it live, And after the desired event happens, they quickly try to bet on it before it's updated. While this could work, they will kick you out if they see you making bets on the spot, and you could get into some serious trouble. But there's nothing stopping you from popping in an airpod, hopping on a call with a homie and once someone scores, naturally cheering, WOAH THEY SCORED LET'S GO I LOVE SPORTS and having your friend quickly make that bet for you. However, the bookies can pretty easily detect your unusual betting pattern, and effectively ban your account."
